= Command Discovery Patterns

This chapter documents the patterns discovered during the exploration of WAFT's command ecosystem.

== Discovery Process

=== Initial Exploration
- User executed various commands
- Tested command capabilities
- Explored command options
- Documented findings

=== Pattern Recognition
- Identified command categories
- Noted common structures
- Discovered integration points
- Mapped relationships

== Key Patterns

=== Pattern 1: Command Categories

Commands naturally group into categories:
- *[Documentation]*: Checkpoint, dossier, one-pager
- *[Learning]*: Study, science-bitch
- *[Generation]*: Worldbuild, tell-story
- *[Status]*: Show-me, visualize
- *[Evolution]*: Evolve-a-ui

=== Pattern 2: Document Generation

Many commands generate documents:
- PDF outputs (checkpoint, dossier, one-pager)
- HTML outputs (show-me, visualize)
- Markdown outputs (work efforts, checkpoints)
- Typst outputs (worldbuild, tell-story)

=== Pattern 3: Scientific Method Integration

Several commands use scientific method:
- `/study` - Scientific learning
- `/science-bitch` - Full workflow
- Evidence-based approaches
- State capture and analysis

=== Pattern 4: Status and Overview

Multiple ways to view project state:
- `/checkpoint` - Status snapshot
- `/dossier` - Comprehensive report
- `/show-me` - Session overview
- `/visualize` - Interactive dashboard

== Discovery Insights

=== Scattered Tools
- Commands exist but are scattered
- No unified interface
- Knowledge required to use
- Output fragmentation

=== Need for Dashboard
- Centralized command access
- Unified status view
- Document management
- Work tracking

== Lessons Learned

=== Command Documentation
- Commands well-documented
- Clear usage examples
- Integration details provided
- Philosophy explained

=== System Integration
- Commands integrate well
- Shared infrastructure
- Consistent patterns
- Extensible design

== Future Patterns

=== Dashboard Pattern
- Centralized interface
- Unified access
- Status aggregation
- Document management

=== Discovery Pattern
- Command registry
- Automatic discovery
- Category organization
- Search and filter
